Sketchpad, a light pen drawing program for the Type 340
// A light pen drawing program for the Type 340 display, after Ivan Sutherland's Sketchpad. A
// menu bar of light pen labels runs across the top, a tracking target follows the pen through
// the display's pen prediction, and the picture (points, lines, circle arcs, texts, numbers and
// instances of masters, held by constraints, with a truss analysis) is kept as a Type 340
// display list.
// Starts at boot, at 100, which opens the extend window and enters the main bank, bank 4.
// Needs banks 0 to 15, the BBN timesharing clock (IOT 32) for its 1 ms counter, the Type 550
// Microtape to keep pictures, and the Type 23 drum for its overlays, which ovlload writes from
// sketchpad.ovl before the program starts (Docs/UsingOverlays.md). Includes
// TYPE340/type340alt.ah (the 340's dra and dss are t340dra and t340dss, since the drum's IOTs
// share those names), LIGHTPEN/lightpen.ah, CLOCK/clockdefs.ah, MICROTAPE/type550defs.ah,
// TYPE340/trackingTarget.ah and the overlay manager, DRUM/overlay.ac; the target's words follow
// trackingTarget.ac's shape. The constants are in sketchpad.ah and the intensities in
// intensities.ah, beside this file.
// Banks. 0 holds the break routine, the frame and every display word but the line slots, which
// alone fill bank 1. 2 holds the arc module, deletion and merging, and Define's geometry; 3 the
// point, line, instance and scalar tables, the dispatch tables and the texts' list; 4 the main
// bank, with the start-up, the main loop, the menus and the modes; 5 the masters' records'
// window MW, then their attachers, the master directory and the constraints' arms' list; 6 the
// overlay window W, with the tape module, the
// scale module and the pen keyboard, root and overlay parts, start-up's gates, the menu census,
// the overlay manager and its table; 7 the instance module and the menu rows' answers; 8 the
// constraint module; 9 its table, the solver's point tables and the places kept for Undo; 10 the
// text module and the instance table; 11 the truss's analysis, its floating point and the lock's
// display; 12 the break-time helpers and the view; 13 the truss's data and
// readouts, the constraints' marks, the line search and the arcs through the view; 14 and 15
// the truss's matrix.
// The code is in the sp*.ac files beside this one, each included where its bank stands, in
// memory order. This file keeps bank 0's variables, the other banks' tables and the bank
// directives.
// The user guide is UsingSketchpad.md and the design SketchpadTechnicalDesign.md, beside this
// file.
//
// 18-Oct-2026 Claude: first release.
// 18-Oct-2026 Claude: production cleanup, comments only.
// 4-Nov-2026 Version 2.0 adding the remainder of the thesis operations
// 11-Nov-2026 Version 2.2 a number of limits were increased

#include <TYPE340/type340alt.ah>
#include <LIGHTPEN/lightpen.ah>
#include <CLOCK/clockdefs.ah>
#include <MICROTAPE/type550defs.ah>
#include <PLOTTER/plotterdefs.ah>

// The brightness of each kind of thing drawn, the tracking target's among them; before
// trackingTarget.ah, which defaults TARGETINTENSITY only if it is not defined.
#include "intensities.ah"

// Every other constant, and the BOXAT macro, the target's arm and scale among them; before
// trackingTarget.ah, which defaults what is not defined.
#include "sketchpad.ah"
#include <TYPE340/trackingTarget.ah>

// The drum's tracks the overlays keep off, the lowest, where drumupdater's programs and
// Z-machine stories go first; the overlays, eight of code and sixteen masters' records, take the
// tracks above it (the owner, 21-Oct-2026: every track may be used, from the top down), where
// am1 places them: W's ten a track each from 11 to 22, the records in the room they leave and
// two a track on 23 to 27, leaving 30 to 37 for later overlays (sketchpad.lst's overlay table
// has the layout).
%%drumreserve 0-10

// Bank 0's variables, those penISR and the routines beside it use.
// Mailboxes written by penISR, copied and cleared for the main loop by snapshot, with the break
// masked.
// menuArmed is set when a menu hit follows REARM frame ends with none; frameAt is the clock's
// reading at the latest frame end.
var frameTicks, frameAt
var menuHits, menuX, menuY, menuArmed
var tgtHits, tgtX, tgtY

// Kept by penISR from frame to frame, frame ends since the last menu hit, saturating at REARM,
// target presentations since the last target hit, saturating at LOSTMIN, counted from the
// second frame end after it (the hit's own frame's are taken off: trackMiss starts at minus
// callsPerFrame), and the clock's reading at the last target hit (the main loop also sets it
// when it restarts the count, trackMiss at 0).
// lastTgt is 1 when the pen's last hit was the target's, 0 once a menu, list or keyboard hit
// has come after it, whatever the main loop's snapshot holds: a loss at 0 is no lift in any
// mode (checkLost drops the stroke first), so the pen jumped to Stop deletes nothing and the
// target carried to the bar commits, fixes or sizes nothing, and Pan's and Center's loss at 0
// only notes the start again (the view module's vwEntry), so the trip moves no view.
var menuGap, trackMiss, lastHitAt, lastTgt

// Nonzero while the target is displayed; penISR moves the target only then.
var tracking

// Nonzero while a list is open; penISR then posts hits below the bar as menu hits.
var listOpen

// frameGo is where penISR, the watchdog and init start the display, the frame or the pen
// keyboard's list while it is open. kbOn is nonzero while the keyboard is open, when penISR
// posts every hit as a menu hit (spkbd.ac).
var frameGo, kbOn

// Nonzero while the truss's readouts are shown, when penISR starts their list (roList, bank 13)
// at the frame's closing halt. The analysis (sptruss.ac) sets and clears it.
var roOn

// The texts' list to start at the frame's closing halt, before the readouts, 0 for none. It is
// one of the text module's two buffers in bank 3, which its txSync sets.
var txGo

// Nonzero while the constraints' arms are shown, when penISR starts their list (arList, bank 5)
// at the frame's closing halt, before the texts'. The marks module's arBegin (bank 13) and the
// view module's arOne (bank 12) set and clear it.
var arGo

// Menu hits in the frame being drawn, kept by penISR.
var frameMenuHits

// Diagnostic counters kept by penISR. strayCount counts breaks with no display flag while the
// display runs, lateCount closing halts whose stop flag showed late, and multiFrames frames with
// two or more menu hits.
var edgeCount, strayCount, lateCount, multiFrames

// The breaks with no display flag taken while the overlay manager is loading (its ovLoading),
// counted by penISR as the drum's.
var drumBreaks

// The main loop's copy of the mailboxes, taken by snapshot.
var sTicks, sFrameAt, sMenuHits, sMenuX, sMenuY, sMenuArmed, sTgtHits, sTgtX, sTgtY

// Target presentations per frame, which penISR counts down.
var callsPerFrame

// An end pair posted by rebuildDisplay for penISR to write, its address (0 when none is
// waiting) and its two words; and bandPost, the arc band's words the arc module posted for
// penISR to write (commitFlip), 0 when none are waiting.
var flipAt, flipW0, flipW1, bandPost

// The target's arms drawn now (tgtKey, clipTarget's key), and a move penISR posted for tgtFlip
// because it changes them (tgtPend set, the new key, and the center's two words). tgtLX and
// tgtLY are the last hit's center words, which penISR has placed or posted; placeTarget clears
// tgtLX, since its move to the middle keeps the arms the last hit left.
var tgtKey, tgtNewKey, tgtPend, tgtPY, tgtPX, tgtLX, tgtLY

// The drawing list in bank 1, three display blocks moved from bank 0 for room, then the master
// store's region 1. The list's line slots, target calls and end-of-list jump are all written at
// run time. All are placed ahead of the code so that every reference to them is a backward one,
// which keeps their address literals out of am1's forward-reference pool defect. The frame
// enters the list from call0; the line list's end jumps to the arc list in bank 0. The 340's
// subroutine words reach both banks, and a save made here returns here, one made from bank 0
// to bank 0. The CPU only stores into the list, by full address, from the main bank, whose
// extend window is open, and from bank 2 inside a window. Every bank but 0 is free from its
// first word.
bank 1
0/
drawList,
    table DRAWLISTSIZE, 0

// The arc band, written at run time by the main bank and bank 2 (sparcs.ac), every reference
// to it tagged :1. bandGate (spframe.ac) enters it once the arc's start is placed; it jumps back
// to bank 0's band for the radius.
arcBand,
    table BANDWORDS + 2, 0

// The circle every constraint glyph draws by save (spframe.ac's GLYPH and gOTail), out to the
// right, then 16 chords round, ending FIXR right of the center (the vectors are for a radius of
// 10). The save returns to bank 0.
gRing, scale(DRAWSCALE) intensity(MARKINTENSITY) lpoff next(vector)
    deltax(FIXR) deltay(0) right
    deltax(1) deltay(4) left up visible
    deltax(2) deltay(3) left up visible
    deltax(3) deltay(2) left up visible
    deltax(4) deltay(1) left up visible
    deltax(4) deltay(1) left down visible
    deltax(3) deltay(2) left down visible
    deltax(2) deltay(3) left down visible
    deltax(1) deltay(4) left down visible
    deltax(1) deltay(4) right down visible
    deltax(2) deltay(3) right down visible
    deltax(3) deltay(2) right down visible
    deltax(4) deltay(1) right down visible
    deltax(4) deltay(1) right up visible
    deltax(3) deltay(2) right up visible
    deltax(2) deltay(3) right up visible
    deltax(1) deltay(4) right up visible end

// The screen during a transfer, a self-contained block started by the tape module and cut off by
// tapeCall's dla of the frame. It draws WAIT, then eight invisible vectors out and back, then
// round again, with no halt, since the CPU polls the tape with the break system off and cannot
// restart it. Each word fetched steals a CPU cycle; the vectors, 127 steps at 1.5 us for one
// fetch each, make the loop about 15 fetches in 1.8 ms, about 4% of the tape loop's cycles.
waitList, WAITPARAM
    y(WAITY) next(point)
    x(WAITX) next(character)
    type340 "WAIT"
    scale(0) lpoff next(vector)
    deltax(0d127) deltay(0) right
    deltax(0d127) deltay(0) left
    deltax(0d127) deltay(0) right
    deltax(0d127) deltay(0) left
    deltax(0d127) deltay(0) right
    deltax(0d127) deltay(0) left
    deltax(0d127) deltay(0) right
    deltax(0d127) deltay(0) left end
    lpoff next(subroutine)
    jump waitList:1 next(parameter)

// The master store's region 1, MPOOL1 words, to the bank's last 4 (sketchpad.ah, the masters'
// comment); region 0 is masters, in bank 0. Written by Define, its store's compaction and Load.
mpool1,
    table MPOOL1, 0

// The point and line tables in bank 3, with the drag's point marks. Ahead of the code for the
// same reason as the drawing list. The main bank and bank 2 reach them through a pointer made
// from their 16-bit address, bank 2 inside an extend window.
bank 3
0/
// Point table, raster coordinates, each axis's table followed by the instances' origins on that
// axis (NVAR words in all). instCount and each instance's master are in bank 10. The tie lists
// follow the scales, so that iScale and iTie are NATT + 1 tables MAXINST apart (instRemove).
pointX,
    table MAXPTS, 0
iX,
    table MAXINST, 0
pointY,
    table MAXPTS, 0
iY,
    table MAXINST, 0

// Line table, point indices.
lineFrom,
    table MAXLINES, 0
lineTo,
    table MAXLINES, 0

// The points that move with a drag (arcPick, arcDrag, and the instance module's carry,
// instPick), a mark for each, nonzero for a point that moves. Define's map borrows it
// (instMap).
ptMark,
    table MAXPTS, 0

// Each instance's cycle flag, 1 while it cycles (Change > Cycle). It stands before iScale and
// the tie lists, MAXINST apart as they are, so that instRemove moves the three together. A scale
// word holds the 340's scale k in its low two bits (IKMASK) and a multiplier code c above, the
// size 2^k times c / 2^15, c = 0 meaning exactly 2^k.
iCyc,
    table MAXINST, 0
iScale,
    table MAXINST, 0
iTie,
    table NATT * MAXINST, 0
// A copy's attachers' points while they merge at its drop, NOPOINT otherwise. Right after the
// tie lists, so that conRen, which renames the tie lists, renames them too.
cpMrg,
    table NATT, NOPOINT
// The designated points, in order, while a copy's attachers merge into them at its drop,
// NOPOINT otherwise. Right after cpMrg, so that conRen renames them too and copyMerge empties
// both together.
desPt,
    table NATT, NOPOINT
// Each canvas text's anchor while it is digits, NOPOINT for a plain text and for every text
// from the text module's txN on. Right after desPt, so that conRen renames them too.
txAn,
    table NTEXT, NOPOINT
// Each canvas text's scalar while it is digits; then the scalars, scN of them, each its value in
// thousandths of an inch and 1 while it is fixed (a value typed). The text module writes them
// through their 16-bit addresses, and the constraint module's D and Y write scVal; the main
// bank's findNearPoint reads scN. txAn to scFix is one run, which a save writes and a load reads
// whole (sptape.ac, TPDIGITS).
txSv,
    table NTEXT, 0
scN, 0
scVal,
    table NSCAL, 0
scFix,
    table NSCAL, 0
// The constraint module's words for the scalars. Each scalar's D's and Y's, counted when the
// sets are built; each scalar's value kept for Undo of an entry (cSnap); and each entry's
// scalar, by its place in the table, NOPOINT for one that names none (cScBind).
scDN,
    table NSCAL, 0
scYN,
    table NSCAL, 0
uScV,
    table NSCAL, 0
cScOf,
    table NCON, NOPOINT

// Three of the main bank's tables, each item's count, a drag's lines and the rebuild's stale
// marks, all reached through a 16-bit address.
// Item number -> times acted on.
itemCount,
    table NITEMS, 0

// Move: the lines on the point being dragged, as line indices.
dragLines,
    table MAXDRAG, 0

// Line indices whose slots the next rebuild writes; staleN of them are in use.
staleList,
    table NSTALE, 0

// The main bank's dispatch tables, the rest of them in spdispatch.ac, included below. The main
// bank reads each through a 16-bit address, its window open, and calls the routine a word names
// by its low 12 bits, in the main bank.
// Where row i's band starts. A hit at or above it, and below row i-1's, is on row i. A
// sublist's rows take the bands from its owning row's on, to row 13, the last any sublist
// reaches (Keep's).
rowThr,
    ROWY0 - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d2 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d3 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d4 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d5 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d6 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d7 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d8 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d9 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d10 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d11 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d12 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d13 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP

// Bar column -> its action, called via jsp.
barTable,
    actOpen:4           // Draw
    actOpen:4           // Edit
    actOpen:4           // Picture
    actOpen:4           // Misc
    actLocate:4
    actUndo:4
    actStop:4
    actOpen:4           // View

// Item number -> its action, called via jsp once its list has closed.
itemAct,
    actLine:4           // Draw: Line
    actCircle:4         // Draw: Circle
    nothing:4           // Draw: Truss, which owns a sublist
    actText:4           // Draw: Text
    nothing:4           // Draw: Dim, which owns a sublist
    actMove:4           // Edit: Move
    actDelete:4         // Edit: Delete
    nothing:4           // Edit: Constr, which owns a sublist
    nothing:4           // Edit: Size, which owns a sublist
    nothing:4           // Edit: Scale, which owns a sublist
    nothing:4           // Edit: Change, which owns a sublist
    actDism:4           // Edit: Dismem
    nothing:4           // Edit: Keep, which owns a sublist
    actKb:4             // Picture: Define, the masters' picker
    actKb:4             // Picture: Inst, likewise
    actKb:4             // Picture: Copy, likewise
    actClear:4          // Picture: Clear
    actTie:4            // Picture: Tie
    actDes:4            // Picture: Desig
    actKb:4             // Picture: Name, the masters' picker, then the name keyboard
    actSize:4           // Size: x1
    actSize:4           // Size: x2
    actSize:4           // Size: x4
    actSize:4           // Size: x8
    actTape:4           // Misc: Save, the tape module's steps (tapeStep)
    actTape:4           // Misc: Load, likewise
    nothing:4           // Misc: Drive, which owns a sublist
    actTape:4           // Misc: Dir, likewise
    actDelCons:4        // Misc: Del cons
    actUnfix:4          // Misc: Unfix
    nothing:4           // Misc: Library, which owns a sublist
    actTape:4           // Misc: Plot, the tape module's steps too, to the plot (spplot.ac)
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D1
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D2
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D3
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D4
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D5
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D6
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D7
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D8
    actHorv:4           // Constr: Horv
    actCons:4           // Constr: Equal
    actCons:4           // Constr: Paral
    actCons:4           // Constr: Perp
    actCons:4           // Constr: Length
    actCons:4           // Constr: Mid
    actFix:4            // Constr: Fix
    actShow:4           // Constr: Show
    actCons:4           // Truss: Beam
    actCons:4           // Truss: Load
    actRoller:4         // Truss: Roller
    actCons:4           // Truss: Axis
    actForces:4         // Truss: Forces
    actCons:4           // Truss: Stiff
    actKb:4             // Change: Master, the masters' picker
    actCycle:4          // Change: Cycle
    actKb:4             // Change: Dwell, the masters' picker
    actKb:4             // Change: Seq
    actNumber:4         // Dim: Number
    actCons:4           // Dim: Dist
    actCons:4           // Dim: Change
    actCons:4           // Dim: Gap
    actScale:4          // Dim: Size, Scale mode's, as Keep's rows (scActOv)
    actView:4           // View: x1
    actView:4           // View: x2
    actView:4           // View: x4
    actView:4           // View: x8
    actPan:4            // View: Pan
    actCenter:4         // View: Center
    actTape:4           // Library: Load, the library's steps (libStep)
    actTape:4           // Library: Save, likewise
    actTape:4           // Library: Dir, likewise
    actTape:4           // Library: Delete, likewise
    actScale:4          // Keep: x1/3, Scale mode's (scActOv)
    actScale:4          // Keep: x1/2
    actScale:4          // Keep: x1
    actScale:4          // Keep: x2
    actScale:4          // Keep: x3
    actScale:4          // Keep: Full
    actScale:4          // Keep: Inch
    actScale:4          // Scale: Part, the overlay scale (scActOv)
    actScale:4          // Scale: Figure, the overlay gscale (spgscale.ac)
    actScale:4          // Scale: All, likewise

// Constr's rows from ICONS1, Truss's after them, and Dim's Dist, Change and Gap past Change's
// and Number -> the constraint mode's type.
rowCons,
    CTEQ                // Equal
    CTPAR               // Paral
    CTPERP              // Perp
    CTLEN               // Length
    CTMID               // Mid
    0                   // Fix, which has its own action
    0                   // Show, likewise
    CTBEAM              // Truss: Beam
    CTLOAD              // Truss: Load
    0                   // Truss: Roller, which has its own action
    CTROLL              // Truss: Axis, a roller's axis
    0                   // Truss: Forces, which has its own action
    CTSTIFF             // Truss: Stiff, a member's stiffness
    table IDIM + 1 - (ICONS1 + 0d13), 0 // Change's rows and Dim's Number, each its own action
    CTDIST              // Dim: Dist
    CTCHG               // Dim: Change
    CTGAP               // Dim: Gap

// The prompts of the number keyboards for Change's Seq, the truss's Stiff and Keep's Inch, whose
// blocks are in bank 6's root (stBlk, cySqBlk, szBlk).
cyPrmS, type340 "Sequence"
stPrm, type340 "Stiffness"
szPrm, type340 "Inches"

// The status word's text for a failed load, nine characters as the tape's are (sptape.ac,
// tpMsgs), which spinit.ac's drumFail copies through its 16-bit address.
drumText, type340 "DRUM     "

// The constraints on size (spsize.ac, spscale.ac's szSolveOv). What asks for a solve, szDirty, and
// the source's word before; whether its entry is new; the row, szKind; the first thing picked; an
// entry's words on their way to the table, szTy. Then the solve's: its place among the instances,
// sizeArg kept, whether it is going back, the new scale words and those they replace, SZSAME
// where unchanged, and whether uSz belongs to Undo's last USCALE record.
szDirty, 0
szPrev, 0
szNew, 0
szKind, 0
szA, 0
szIdx, 0
szArg, 0
szRet, 0
szUG, 0
szTy,
    table CW, 0
szW,
    table MAXINST, 0
uSz,
    table MAXINST, 0

// An unused mark block's words, which markUnused copies; markWrite then writes the positions
// and the gates. Each cross is its point's words and a save of bank 0's mkCross.
markTpl,
    scale(DRAWSCALE) intensity(MARKINTENSITY) lpoff next(subroutine)
    jump markEnd:0 next(parameter)
    y(0) next(point)
    x(0) next(subroutine)
    save mkCross:0 next(vector)
    lpoff next(point)
    y(0) next(point)
    x(0) next(subroutine)
    save mkCross:0 next(vector)
    lpoff next(subroutine)
    jump markEnd:0 next(parameter)
    y(0) next(point)
    x(0) next(subroutine)
    save mkCross:0 next(vector)

#include "spdispatch.ac"

// For each truss member, nonzero when an end is a roller on an axis not level (taMI), and its
// Beam parameter word, its stiffness (taMK), which the truss module reaches likewise.
taMI,
    table NCON, 0
taMK,
    table NCON, 0

// Ten of the truss module's three-word numbers (spfloat.ac), which it reaches likewise. The
// pivot being formed and the quotient l of the factorization (taD, taL), 1/L's two inputs (drX,
// drY) and a member's six products (asP1 to asP6, through asPrT and asTab).
taD,
    table 3, 0
taL,
    table 3, 0
drX,
    table 3, 0
drY,
    table 3, 0
asP1,
    table 3, 0
asP2,
    table 3, 0
asP3,
    table 3, 0
asP4,
    table 3, 0
asP5,
    table 3, 0
asP6,
    table 3, 0

// Each instance hidden by the view, nonzero while its figure is not wholly on the screen or
// would pass x8. Written by the instance module's instView, read only while the view is
// magnified, by the lock and the texts' list.
iHid,
    table MAXINST, 0

// Each constraint mark's slot hidden by the view, nonzero while the place it marks is off the
// screen. Written by the marks module's mkMarks for slot j, read by its mkNear, which passes
// over a hidden mark. All 0 at x1.
mkHid,
    table NCON, 0

// Each constraint's rank on its line, for a mark that stands on one: how many entries before it
// in the table name the same line; or on its point, for a mark that stands on one point (F, A,
// a designation, a roller's O): how many such entries before it name the same point; or at its
// place, for a two-line mark (E, P, R): how many such marks before it stand there. Counted
// again by the overlay ranks (spranks.ac) only when the table has changed (mkRkOld, set by bank
// 8's cBuild), and read by the marks module's cMkPos, so that writing the marks while points
// move does not count them again.
mkRank,
    table NCON, 0

// A designation's digit's call, by rank, the marks module's (mkGlyph).
cDgTab,
    save gD1:0 next(subroutine)
    save gD2:0 next(subroutine)
    save gD3:0 next(subroutine)
    save gD4:0 next(subroutine)
    save gD5:0 next(subroutine)
    save gD6:0 next(subroutine)

// Each point's rays, for a one-point mark's place: 0400000 while the point carries a one-point
// mark, with bit r (1 << r) set for each line leaving it in ray r, r * 22.5 degrees
// counterclockwise from level. Written by the marks module's mkRays at each writing of the
// marks, read by its cMkPos, and cleared by its mkMarks when the writing is done, so 0 between
// writings.
ptRay,
    table MAXPTS, 0

// Each truss member's coefficients on its ends' horizontal or axis unknowns, A's then B's,
// three-word numbers, which the truss module (sptruss.ac) writes and reads through its 16-bit
// address.
tdC,
    table NCON * 6, 0

// Copy's store, in bank 5 with the constraints' arms' list after it: the window MW, where one
// master's record is resident at a time (sketchpad.ah, Copy's store), and the root's words after
// it. The record's tables are labeled here, at their places in the window, with no words: its
// points relative to its origin from cpX and cpY, its lines, indices into those points, from
// cpFrom and cpTo, its arcs as the arc table holds them, from cpC to cpK, CPARCS apart, its
// constraints from cpCon, CW words each, its display words from mrWords, and its sub-instances
// from cpSub, SUBW words each (sketchpad.ah, NSUB). Written by Define
// (the instance module's instDefOv) and read by Copy, a dismember and Define's instances in
// banks 2, 7 and 8, through 16-bit addresses, once mrLoad has made the master's record
// resident. Ahead of the code for the same reason as the drawing list. MW is twopass: an
// eviction writes the outgoing record back, then reads the incoming one, so a halt during the
// write is retried and loses no part of the user's drawing (Docs/UsingOverlays.md, "The swap and
// the twopass window"); am1 packs the records on the drum at their own length.
bank 5
0/
%%window MW, 0, MRECW + 1, twopass
2/
cpX,
2 + CPPTS/
cpY,
2 + 2 * CPPTS/
cpFrom,
2 + 2 * CPPTS + CPLINES/
cpTo,
2 + 2 * CPPTS + 2 * CPLINES/
cpC,
2 + 2 * CPPTS + 2 * CPLINES + CPARCS/
cpS,
2 + 2 * CPPTS + 2 * CPLINES + 2 * CPARCS/
cpE,
2 + 2 * CPPTS + 2 * CPLINES + 3 * CPARCS/
cpD,
2 + 2 * CPPTS + 2 * CPLINES + 4 * CPARCS/
cpK,
2 + 2 * CPPTS + 2 * CPLINES + CPATAB * CPARCS/
cpCon,
2 + 2 * CPPTS + 2 * CPLINES + CPATAB * CPARCS + NCPCON * CW/
mrWords,
2 + 2 * CPPTS + 2 * CPLINES + CPATAB * CPARCS + NCPCON * CW + MPOOL1/
cpSub,

// The records, one a master, packed on the drum at their own length, MW being twopass. Assembled
// empty: a record is read only for a master Define has made, which writes it whole.
%%overlay mrec0, MW, persistent
    export mrc0
mrc0,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay
%%overlay mrec1, MW, persistent
    export mrc1
mrc1,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay
%%overlay mrec2, MW, persistent
    export mrc2
mrc2,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay
%%overlay mrec3, MW, persistent
    export mrc3
mrc3,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay
%%overlay mrec4, MW, persistent
    export mrc4
mrc4,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay
%%overlay mrec5, MW, persistent
    export mrc5
mrc5,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay
%%overlay mrec6, MW, persistent
    export mrc6
mrc6,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay
%%overlay mrec7, MW, persistent
    export mrc7
mrc7,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay
%%overlay mrec8, MW, persistent
    export mrc8
mrc8,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay
%%overlay mrec9, MW, persistent
    export mrc9
mrc9,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay
%%overlay mrec10, MW, persistent
    export mrc10
mrc10,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay
%%overlay mrec11, MW, persistent
    export mrc11
mrc11,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay
%%overlay mrec12, MW, persistent
    export mrc12
mrc12,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay
%%overlay mrec13, MW, persistent
    export mrc13
mrc13,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay
%%overlay mrec14, MW, persistent
    export mrc14
mrc14,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay
%%overlay mrec15, MW, persistent
    export mrc15
mrc15,
    table MRECW, 0
%%endoverlay

// Master k's attachers, kept in the root: their master point indices in designation order from
// cpAtt + k * NATT, cpNAtt + k of them, and each one's point's offset from the origin, at x1,
// from cpAX and cpAY + k * NATT, NMASTER * NATT apart (Define writes all four). The solver's T,
// a carry and Change read them while any record, or none, is resident.
MRECW + 2/
cpAtt,
    table NMASTER * NATT, 0
cpAX,
    table NMASTER * NATT, 0
cpAY,
    table NMASTER * NATT, 0
cpNAtt,
    table NMASTER, 0

// The master directory, NMASTER masters, in bank 5 since 16 of each outgrow bank 2: each
// master's length in words, 0 while its slot is empty, then its box relative to its origin.
mLen,
    table NMASTER, 0
mMinX,
    table NMASTER, 0
mMaxX,
    table NMASTER, 0
mMinY,
    table NMASTER, 0
mMaxY,
    table NMASTER, 0

// Copy's part of the directory, CBOXOFF words after the figure's box: the copy box, the
// figure's box widened to take in every point, relative to the origin; then how many points,
// lines and arcs Copy's store holds for each master.
cMinX,
    table NMASTER, 0
cMaxX,
    table NMASTER, 0
cMinY,
    table NMASTER, 0
cMaxY,
    table NMASTER, 0
cpNP,
    table NMASTER, 0
cpNL,
    table NMASTER, 0
cpNA,
    table NMASTER, 0
// Each master's place in the store, its offset in the two regions seen as one (sketchpad.ah,
// the masters' comment); read only while its length is not 0.
mStart,
    table NMASTER, 0

// The masters' nesting, kept in the root so that Define and the loads read it with no record
// resident: each master's sub-instances' count (mNSub); its own words' count (mOwnLen), its
// lines' and arcs', which come first; the count before its own attachers' crosses (mDrawLen), the
// words a master holding it copies; the masters it holds, a bit each, M1 in bit 17 (mUses); and
// its own texts' count (mTxOwn), which come first among its texts, the copies of its
// sub-instances' masters' after them (sptext.ac, txParts).
// One run on the tape (sptape.ac, TPNESTW), right after mStart, so that a failed load empties
// the directory and them as one run (tpWipe).
mNSub,
    table NMASTER, 0
mOwnLen,
    table NMASTER, 0
mDrawLen,
    table NMASTER, 0
mUses,
    table NMASTER, 0
mTxOwn,
    table NMASTER, 0

// The propagation's walk of a master (spdefword.ac, rwBuild), in defdism, which W has no room
// for: its blocks, its own words' and its sub-instances', after their count; its crosses'
// visits, x, y and the beam, after theirs; laid out as Define's (sbN, sbBlk; avN to avV) so that
// defWalk reads either. Written and read within one call of the overlay.
rwSbN, 0
rwBlk,
    table (NSUB + 1) * DBW, 0
rwAvN, 0
rwAvX,
    table 4 * NATT, 0
rwAvY,
    table 4 * NATT, 0
rwAvV,
    table 4 * NATT, 0

// Master rwJ's sub-instances' tie points, in its resident record, moved to their masters'
// attachers (cpAX, cpAY) at each one's scale word from its offset, as Define found them: the
// propagation's commit (spdefword.ac, rwRedo) calls it, since a redefinition may move them. A
// master's own attacher on such a point keeps its place, and a line ending there its words. Here,
// not in defdism, for W's room.
// AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jsp i, from defdism.
rwTies,
    local rtTs, rtTa, rtTn, rtTx, rtEnd, rtRtn, rtN, rtA, rtM, rtC, rtX, rtY, rtH, rtK, rtT, rtQ, \
        rtV, rtP
    dac rtRtn
    lac i [rwJ:2]
    add [mNSub:5]
    dac rtP
    lac i rtP
    sza i               // skip if it has sub-instances
    jmp rtEnd
    cma
    dac rtN
    lac [cpSub:5]
    dac rtA
rtTs,
    lac i rtA           // SBM
    dac rtM
    sal 1s
    add rtM
    sal 1s              // m * NATT, 6
    dac rtC
    lac rtA
    add [SBX]
    dac rtP
    lac i rtP
    dac rtX
    idx rtP
    lac i rtP
    dac rtY
    idx rtP
    lac i rtP           // SBS
    dac rtH
    lac rtM
    add [cpNAtt:5]
    dac rtP
    lac i rtP
    sza i               // skip if its master has attachers
    jmp rtTx
    cma
    dac rtK
    lac rtA
    add [SBT]
    dac rtT
rtTa,
    lac i rtT
    sad [NOPOINT]       // skip if a tie
    jmp rtTn
    dac rtQ
    lac rtC
    add [cpAX:5]
    dac rtP
    lac i rtP
    lio rtH
    dac i [ieSize:7]
    jsp i [ieSize:7+1]
    add rtX
    dac rtV
    lac rtQ
    add [cpX:5]
    dac rtP
    lac rtV
    dac i rtP
    lac rtC
    add [cpAY:5]
    dac rtP
    lac i rtP
    lio rtH
    dac i [ieSize:7]
    jsp i [ieSize:7+1]
    add rtY
    dac rtV
    lac rtQ
    add [cpY:5]
    dac rtP
    lac rtV
    dac i rtP
rtTn,
    idx rtC
    idx rtT
    isp rtK             // skip once every attacher is taken
    jmp rtTa
rtTx,
    lac rtA
    add [SUBW]
    dac rtA
    isp rtN             // skip once every sub-instance is taken
    jmp rtTs
rtEnd,
    jmp i rtRtn
rtRtn, 0
rtN, 0
rtA, 0
rtM, 0
rtC, 0
rtX, 0
rtY, 0
rtH, 0
rtK, 0
rtT, 0
rtQ, 0
rtV, 0
rtP, 0
    endloc

// arcFill's kept offsets (bank 2), vertices 0 to NQ-1 of the circle it fills, each v then u;
// here, not in bank 7, for bank 7's room.
arcOff,
    table 2*NQ, 0

// Scale's record for Undo (spscale.ac): each constraint entry's value before the last scale that
// changed something, 0 for one it did not change. The overlay scale reaches it through its
// 16-bit address. Here, not in bank 11, for bank 11's room.
// The variants' tables (spvar.ac): each one's master, its code c, and its offset in the master
// store, MNOPOOL while free.
vaM,
    table NVARIANT, 0
vaC,
    table NVARIANT, 0
vaO,
    table NVARIANT, MNOPOOL

scUOld,
    table NCON, 0

// The constraints' arms' list, after the store and outside the tape's run of it. A display list
// that penISR starts by dla after the frame's closing halt while arGo is set, since the 340
// jumps only within banks 0 and 1, and which ends in a halt. NCON slots of ARMWORDS, packed,
// slot k the k-th E, P or R entry in the table, and the word after the last used, its parameter
// word's place, the halt. The marks module's arBegin (bank 13) and the view module's arOne
// (bank 12) write it, through 16-bit addresses. Assembled empty.
arList,
    lpoff halt interrupt
    table NCON * ARMWORDS, 0
    lpoff halt interrupt
    halt

// arcKeep's save of the arc module's words arcCX to arcQY (bank 2, spedit.ac), which arcKeep
// reaches inside an extend window.
akSave,
    table AKEEPN, 0

// The masters' picker's screen (its blocks and keys in the tape module's root, sptape.ac, its
// descriptor, codes and hit records in the overlay kbd, spkbd.ac): its title, the sixteen
// lines, taking the pen when lit so that a tap finds them, and Cancel where the keyboard's OK
// is; then its halt. Each line, M1 to M8 down the left and
// M9 to M16 down the right, is a directory's line: its parameter word, which the instance
// module's mpkLines writes lit or dim for the row that opens it, its place, its label and its
// name's run, which mpkLines writes "empty" or blank. It holds no jump or save, as the
// keyboard's list does not.
mpkList,
    KBTXT
    y(KBPY) next(point)
    x(KBX0) next(character)
    type340 "Masters"
mpkL,
    DIRLINE(0, 0, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 1) * 0100 + KCSPACE)
    DIRLINE(1, 0, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 2) * 0100 + KCSPACE)
    DIRLINE(2, 0, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 3) * 0100 + KCSPACE)
    DIRLINE(3, 0, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 4) * 0100 + KCSPACE)
    DIRLINE(4, 0, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 5) * 0100 + KCSPACE)
    DIRLINE(5, 0, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 6) * 0100 + KCSPACE)
    DIRLINE(6, 0, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 7) * 0100 + KCSPACE)
    DIRLINE(7, 0, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 0d8) * 0100 + KCSPACE)
    DIRLINE(0, 1, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 0d9) * 0100 + KCSPACE)
    DIRLINE(1, 1, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 1) * 0100 + KCZERO + 0)
    DIRLINE(2, 1, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 1) * 0100 + KCZERO + 1)
    DIRLINE(3, 1, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 1) * 0100 + KCZERO + 2)
    DIRLINE(4, 1, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 1) * 0100 + KCZERO + 3)
    DIRLINE(5, 1, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 1) * 0100 + KCZERO + 4)
    DIRLINE(6, 1, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 1) * 0100 + KCZERO + 5)
    DIRLINE(7, 1, KCM * 010000 + (KCZERO + 1) * 0100 + KCZERO + 6)
mpkKey, KBKEY
    y(KBYB) next(point)
    x(KBXOK) next(character)
mpkKTxt,
    017 * 010000 + 013 * 0100 + KCUP
    KBPAD
    KBBLANK
mpkHalt, lpoff halt interrupt

// Each Define refusal's word under the bar, for the overlay defdism's instDefNoOv (spinst.ac),
// answers DEFEMPTY (1) to DEFPDIGIT in order. NO ROOM and OFF EDGE are the text module's.
dnTab,
    dnParts:5           // DEFEMPTY, texts alone
    dnFull:5            // DEFFULL
    dnBig:5             // DEFWORDS
    dnSlow:5            // DEFTIME
    dnCons:5            // DEFCONS
    dnCyc:5             // DEFCYCLE
    txWords:012+4*TXSFULL // DEFNROOM, NO ROOM
    txWords:012+4*TXSOFF // DEFNOFF, OFF EDGE
    dnArc:5             // DEFNARC
    txWords:012+4*TXSFULL // DEFTEXT, NO ROOM
    dnMany:5            // DEFNSUB
    dnLoop:5            // DEFLOOP
    dnScale:5           // DEFNSCALE
    dnDig:5             // DEFDIGIT
    dnPBig:5            // DEFPBIG
    dnPSlow:5           // DEFPSLOW
    dnPRoom:5           // DEFPROOM
    dnPDig:5            // DEFPDIGIT

// The words, four each of nine characters, as txWords'. A holder's refusal's first three
// characters are its master's number (dnM1, dnM10).
dnParts, type340 "NO PARTS "
dnFull, type340 "FULL     "
dnBig, type340 "TOO BIG  "
dnSlow, type340 "TOO SLOW "
dnCons, type340 "CONSTR   "
dnCyc, type340 "CYCLING  "
dnArc, type340 "ARC SIZE "
dnMany, type340 "TOO MANY "
dnLoop, type340 "LOOP     "
dnScale, type340 "SCALE    "
dnDig, type340 "DIGITS   "
dnPBig, type340 "    BIG  "
dnPSlow, type340 "    SLOW "
dnPRoom, type340 "    ROOM "
dnPDig, type340 "    DIGIT"
dnM1, type340 " M1"
dnM10, type340 "M10"

// What subBring (spsub.ac) is to bring: for each sub-instance its master and its composed scale
// word, read from the record before the first variant loads another.
svT,
    table 2 * NSUB, 0

#include "splibdir.ac"
bank 0

#include "spbreak.ac"

#include "spframe.ac"

variables
constants

// The main bank holds the start-up, the main loop, the menus, the mode handlers and the drawing
// list's upkeep, with their variables; their tables are in bank 3, and the instance code is bank
// 7's module, entered only through instCall. It runs with the extend window open, so a reference to
// a word in bank 0 (penISR's variables, the display) is made through its 16-bit address,
// OP i [X:0], and one to a table in bank 3 through a pointer made from [X:3]. It is placed
// after banks 0 and 3, so that every reference it makes to them is a backward one.
bank 4
0/
#include "spmain.ac"

#include "spmenus.ac"

#include "spundo.ac"

#include "spmodes.ac"

#include "sppen.ac"

#include "spdisplay.ac"

variables
constants

// The arc module, alone in bank 2. It holds the arcs' geometry, their table, and the words of
// their slots and of the arc band in bank 0; and, since arcs hang on points, the routines that
// remove points and lines, merge and delete; and Define and the master directory, and Copy's
// store and its arcs; the main bank takes a copy's points and lines from the store itself. The
// main bank enters it only through arcCall, with an entry number
// (AEINIT to AEUNDO), and reads Define's words through their 16-bit address; the module runs
// with the extend window closed, opening it only to read the variables of the main bank and
// bank 0 and the tables of banks 3, 5 and 8 and to store into them or the display lists, and it
// calls nothing outside bank 2 but bank 12's lineArc, loadLine and vwCross and bank 13's vaSlot
// and vaBand, each by jsp i [X:01n]. It is placed after banks 0 and 4, so that every reference
// it makes to them is a backward one. After it, two scale words composed and the variants' root
// calls with no room in bank 9 (spvar2.ac), entered by jsp i [X:2] with the window open.
// Vertex k of an arc is its start rotated k steps of 2pi/NARC about the center, worked out
// directly from the start with a quarter-wave table of sines, so no error builds up from step
// to step and a full circle closes exactly on its start. Offsets from the center are kept in
// 32nds of a unit, rounded to a unit only for the display. An arc slot's vectors run backward
// over every s'th vertex down to vertex 0, the start, s whole steps the chord its radius needs
// (arcClass); only the last carries end. The gate enters the last k / s of them for an arc of k
// whole steps, or the word before those, which then holds the part step from the end to vertex
// s (k / s). The band's run the full circle in whole steps.
bank 2
0/

#include "sparcs.ac"

#include "spedit.ac"

#include "spdrag.ac"

#include "spvar2.ac"

#include "sparcdata.ac"

constants

// The drum overlay manager (Docs/UsingOverlays.md), at bank 11's first words, ahead of bank 6
// in the source, since it must come before the first %%ovcall. The rest of bank 11 follows bank
// 10, below.
bank 0d11
0/

#include <DRUM/overlay.ac>

// Bank 6 begins with the drum overlays' window W (sketchpad.ah), where the overlay manager reads
// an overlay from the drum when it is called and W holds another. The overlays are tape
// (sptape.ac), library, the library of masters (splib.ac), plot, Plot (spplot.ac), scale
// (spscale.ac), kbd (spkbd.ac), gscale (spgscale.ac), defdism, Define and Dismember (spinst.ac),
// copy, Copy's drop's arcs and merges (spdefine.ac), ranks (spranks.ac), and truss, the truss's
// analysis (sptruss.ac and spfloat.ac); gscale and truss are persistent. Each is entered only
// through root code, bank 6's for scale and kbd, bank 5's loop gsRun for gscale, bank 7's for
// defdism, bank 2's for copy, bank 13's mkMarks for ranks and bank 11's for tape, library, plot
// and truss, the stubs keeping the entries' names, so their callers call them as they always
// have. The root
// follows W: the scale module's (spscale.ac), Edit > Scale and its mode, entered
// by the main bank's gates; then the pen keyboard's (spkbd.ac), entered by its four entries,
// whose list is in W. Each keeps here the words its overlay reaches directly.
bank 6
0/
%%window W, OVWFIRST, OVWLAST
OVWLAST+1/

#include "spscale.ac"

#include "spkbd.ac"

#include "spgscale.ac"

// The number keyboard's blocks for Change's Seq, the truss's Stiff and Keep's Inch, as Dwell's in
// spinst.ac; their prompts are in bank 3. The keyboard reads both through their 16-bit
// addresses. The instance module opens the first two and bank 12's szKbGo the third.
stBlk, KBDEC
    STIFFDIG
    stPrm:3
    cyBuf:7
    stDone:4
    0
cySqBlk, KBDEC
    NSEQ
    cyPrmS:3
    cyBuf:7
    ckDone:4
    0
szBlk, KBDEC
    SZDIGS
    szPrm:3
    cyBuf:7
    szKbDone:014
    0

// An O's parameter by its digits' scale, x1 to x8 (cScBind), the gap in 32nds, with CUNUSED's
// sign bit set, as a Length's is. Read by the constraint module through its 16-bit address; here
// for bank 5's room.
cGapTab,
    CUNUSED + (GAPHALF + GAPMARGIN) * 0d32
    CUNUSED + (0d2 * GAPHALF + GAPMARGIN) * 0d32
    CUNUSED + (0d4 * GAPHALF + GAPMARGIN) * 0d32
    CUNUSED + (0d8 * GAPHALF + GAPMARGIN) * 0d32

constants

// Bank 2's second part, after its first's constants: the gates through which defdism's Define
// words and the overlay copy call bank 2, and the overlay copy's root stubs, with the overlay
// itself, Copy's drop's arcs and merges, run in W (spdefine.ac). Here, after the manager and W,
// since a stub's %%ovcall must follow the manager and an overlay its window.
bank 2

#include "spdefine.ac"

// The library's trial's refusals, DEFPBIG to DEFPDIGIT, as the library's tape statuses, read by
// splib.ac's root through its 16-bit address. Here for bank 11's room.
lyMap,
    TSTOOBIG
    TSSLOW
    TSNOROOM
    TSDIGIT

constants

// The instance module, in bank 7. It keeps the instance list's slots in bank 0, and adds,
// places, moves, locks, sizes and removes an instance. The main bank enters it only through
// instCall, with an entry number
// (IEINIT to IEVIEW; the view module enters it too, for IEVIEW), and writes litInst at init
// through its 16-bit address; it runs with the extend window open, reaching the main bank's
// variables, the master directory in bank 2 and the instance tables in banks 3 and 10 through
// 16-bit addresses, and calls nothing outside bank 7 but the text module's entries for it (bank
// 10) and the view module's vwBox (bank 12), as spinst.ac's header says. Define and Dismember
// are its overlay defdism, run in W from their stubs here, which keep the entries' names; every
// word defdism keeps between calls is this bank's. It is placed last, so
// that every reference it makes to the other banks is a backward one.
bank 7
0/

#include "spinst.ac"

constants

// The constraint module's tables, alone in bank 9, the places it keeps for Undo and the point
// tables it works on. The module reaches them through their 16-bit addresses, and bank 2's
// ptMarked and the main bank's conRedraw read cFlag so. Placed before bank 8, so that every
// reference the module makes to them is a backward one. Each point table has a word for each of
// the solver's variables (NVAR), the points' and then the instances' origins'.
bank 0d9
0/

// Every point's place when an entry was added (cSnap), read back by cUndo.
uSX,
    table NVAR, 0
uSY,
    table NVAR, 0

// Each point's flags: FIN while it is the solver's, FFIX while it is fixed, FMOV while it is
// moved by the last publish (cPublish) or put back by Undo (cUndo), and FTCH while this pass's
// sweeps have touched it (cTouch). Bank 2's ptMarked reads FMOV in place of ptMark while the arc
// module works out the arcs on the moved points (conArcs), and conRedraw reads it.
cFlag,
    table NVAR, 0

// The points this pass's sweeps touched, once each, in the order touched (cTouch); cPublish
// then compacts the ones it moved to the front, cMovN of them, which carry the FMOV marks, and
// so do the points Undo put back (cUndo). The next pass clears the marks from the front alone
// (cUnmark).
cPub,
    table NVAR, 0

// The working values, in 32nds of a unit, of the solver's points.
wX,
    table NVAR, 0
wY,
    table NVAR, 0

// Where the last publish found each point it moved, or Undo each point it put back, for
// cRevert.
oX,
    table NVAR, 0
oY,
    table NVAR, 0

// The solver's points (cBuild).
cIn,
    table NVAR, 0

// The ties the solver keeps (cBuild), each tie's place in the tie lists, a * MAXINST + i.
cTies,
    table NATT * MAXINST, 0

// Each entry's lines' lengths, in 32nds, as the last sweep found or set them, two words an entry
// by its place in the table (line A-B's, then line C-D's). An E's or an L's root starts from them
// (cProjM). A place another entry has taken since only costs that root more steps (cHyp). A C
// entry keeps its circle's radius in its first word likewise (cProjK, cRim).
cLast,
    table NCON * 2, 0

// Each arc's radius, in 32nds, as its implicit C last brought its ends to it, by the arc's index:
// both rays' roots start from it (cProjC, cRim). An arc replaced or renumbered
// since only costs those roots more steps (cHyp).
cArcG,
    table MAXARCS, 0

// How many constraints each master keeps, cpNCon + k of them, in its record's cpCon (bank 5),
// CW words each as the table holds them but in master point indices. Written by Define (the
// instance module's instDef), read by Copy's drop (cCopy) and Define's room (instNest), which
// reads it with no record resident, and saved with each picture (sptape.ac).
cpNCon,
    table NMASTER, 0

// cKeep's slots, a line, a second line and an arc each; and per constraint type, indexed by the
// type word's low bits (CTMASK), how many points it names (A, A and B, A to C, or A to D). The
// arcs the solver keeps, cArcs, are bank 2's (sparcdata.ac).
kpLock,
    table 0d9, 0
cNPts,
    0
    2                   // CTHL
    2                   // CTHP
    1                   // CTF
    4                   // CTEQ
    2                   // CTLEN
    4                   // CTPAR
    4                   // CTPERP
    3                   // CTMID
    3                   // CTON
    3                   // CTONC
    1                   // CTATT
    2                   // CTBEAM
    2                   // CTLOAD
    3                   // CTROLL: its point, then its axis's line
    1                   // CTDES
    3                   // CTDIST: line A-B, then the digits' anchor
    3                   // CTCHG: likewise
    2                   // CTGAP: its point, then the digits' anchor
    2                   // CTSAME: its two instances
    1                   // CTFULL
    1                   // CTINCH
    3                   // CTSZNUM: its instance, again, then the digits' anchor

// Per type, indexed likewise, the mark's call of its glyph; a designation's mark calls instead
// the digit for its place in the order, from cDgTab, designation 1 first (cMarks). No type has
// index 0, so its word holds an E at a ratio's M (mkEq).
cGlyph,
    save gM:0 next(subroutine)
    save gH:0 next(subroutine)
    save gH:0 next(subroutine)
    save gF:0 next(subroutine)
    save gE:0 next(subroutine)
    save gL:0 next(subroutine)
    save gP:0 next(subroutine)
    save gR:0 next(subroutine)
    save gX:0 next(subroutine)
    save gN:0 next(subroutine)
    save gC:0 next(subroutine)
    save gA:0 next(subroutine)
    save gB:0 next(subroutine)
    save gW:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO0:0 next(subroutine)  // a roller's mark is cRlTab's instead (cMarks)
    save gD1:0 next(subroutine)
    save gD:0 next(subroutine)
    save gY:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO:0 next(subroutine)
    save gS:0 next(subroutine)
    save gU:0 next(subroutine)
    save gI:0 next(subroutine)
    save gZ:0 next(subroutine)

// Per direction k (cRlDir: k * 22.5 degrees from level), the y of the mark's offset from its
// place on the line, at right angles to it, in thousandths of the distance (cMkPos scales it,
// quantizing once); its x is cOfX, in bank 13 beside cMkPos, for this bank's room. Above a flat
// line (k 0 to 2, 6, 7), right of a steep one (k 3 to 5), as the truss's readouts stand. The
// cosines and sines of 0, 22.5, 45 and 67.5 degrees.
cOfY,
    0d1000
    0d924
    0d707
    -0d383
    0
    0d383
    0d707
    0d924

// A one-point mark's eight candidate directions (cMkPos), in the order a tie between equally
// clear ones is broken: up, right, down, left, then up-right, down-right, down-left, up-left.
// For each, the bit of its ray in a point's word of ptRay (ray r at r * 22.5 degrees
// counterclockwise from level, so direction d * 45 degrees is ray 2d), and its offset from the
// point in screen units, x then y, FIXR + MKGAP long, so that the circle stands MKGAP clear of
// the point, the diagonals' rounded.
cPtB,
    0d16                // ray 4
    1                   // ray 0
    0d4096              // ray 12
    0d256               // ray 8
    4                   // ray 2
    0d16384             // ray 14
    0d1024              // ray 10
    0d64                // ray 6
cPtX,
    0
    FIXR + MKGAP
    0
    -(FIXR + MKGAP)
    PTDIAG
    PTDIAG
    -PTDIAG
    -PTDIAG
cPtY,
    FIXR + MKGAP
    0
    -(FIXR + MKGAP)
    0
    PTDIAG
    -PTDIAG
    -PTDIAG
    PTDIAG

// Each ray r's bit in a point's word of ptRay, 1 << r (mkRays).
cRyBit,
    1
    2
    4
    0d8
    0d16
    0d32
    0d64
    0d128
    0d256
    0d512
    0d1024
    0d2048
    0d4096
    0d8192
    0d16384
    0d32768

// The constraint table, conTab (spcons.ac's header describes it), cCount, then NCON entries
// of CW words.
conTab,
cCount, 0
cEntries,
    table NCON * CW, 0

// The variants (spvar.ac), root: a master's words at a code c, kept in the master store.
#include "spvar.ac"

// After the table, which menu rows can act (sprows.ac's rowCan), entered by the main bank's menus
// directly, from the census in bank 11.
#include "sprows.ac"

constants

// The constraint module, alone in bank 8, the solver and the sets it works on; its table and
// point tables are in bank 9. The main bank enters it only through conCall, with an entry
// number (CEINIT to CESTSET); it runs with the extend window open, reaching the point, line and
// arc tables, the main bank's variables and its tables in bank 9 through 16-bit addresses, and
// calls nothing outside bank 8 but the marks in bank 13 (spmarks.ac). Bank 2, the main bank and
// the tape module reach its table and words through their 16-bit addresses. It is placed last,
// so that every reference it makes to the other banks is a backward one.
bank 0d8
0/

#include "spcons.ac"

constants

bank 5

// Per type, indexed by the type word's low bits (CTMASK), the projection a sweep runs on it.
// The sweep fetches a word and runs it in bank 8 (cTick's ctJ), the constraint module's, so each
// jsp holds its target's offset alone: a bank tag on the operand would land in the opcode.
cPjTab,
    nop
    MCJSP(cProjH:010)
    MCJSP(cProjH:010)
    nop                 // a fix is nothing to project
    MCJSP(cProjM:010)
    MCJSP(cProjM:010)
    MCJSP(cProjP:010)
    MCJSP(cProjP:010)
    MCJSP(cProjX:010)
    MCJSP(cProjN:010)
    MCJSP(cProjK:010)
    nop                 // an attacher is nothing to project
    nop                 // nor is a beam, a load or a roller: the truss's analysis reads them
    nop
    nop
    nop                 // nor a designation
    MCJSP(cProjD:010)
    MCJSP(cProjY:010)
    MCJSP(cProjM:010)   // an O, as a Length
    nop                 // nor a size's, which a commit acts on (spscale.ac, szSolveOv)
    nop
    nop
    nop

// The leader's vector by the class of the label's length (LEADROW): the longest length in each.
// Read by bank 12's placeBox through its 16-bit address; here for bank 12's room.
leadTab,
    deltax(LEADLEN(3)) deltay(0) left visible end
    deltax(LEADLEN(5)) deltay(0) left visible end
    deltax(LEADLEN(7)) deltay(0) left visible end
    deltax(LEADLEN(0d8)) deltay(0) left visible end

// A roller's mark by its axis's direction, k * 22.5 degrees counterclockwise from level, k 0 to 7
// (the marks module's cRlDir), read by the marks module through its 16-bit address; here for
// bank 9's room.
cRlTab,
    save gO0:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO1:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO2:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO3:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO4:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO5:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO6:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO7:0 next(subroutine)

// The group's scale's root loop (spgscale.ac), here for bank 6's room. Call the overlay gscale's
// entry gsEntOv; while it answers nonzero, having shut the instances' gates and set their new
// sizes, write every instance again from the root (the instance module's IEVIEW), where the
// variants' code builds each new size's words in the store (spvar.ac's vaOf), which it cannot do
// while an overlay runs, and call gsEntOv again to finish.
// AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jsp i [gsRun:5], from spscale.ac's root stubs.
gsRun,
    local grLoop, grRtnW
    dac grRtnW
grLoop,
    %%ovcall gscale, gsEntOv
    sza i               // skip if the instances are to be written again
    jmp i grRtnW
    lio [IEVIEW]
    jsp i [instEntry:7]
    jmp grLoop
grRtnW, 0
    endloc

// The text module, in bank 10 with its tables. The main bank enters it through txCall, the
// instance module and initVars at its entries, by their 16-bit addresses; its list is in bank 3.
bank 0d10
0/

#include "sptext.ac"

// The instance table, instCount instances, each its master; their origins, scales and ties are
// in bank 3. Every user reaches it through its 16-bit address.
instCount, 0
iMaster,
    table MAXINST, 0

// A carry's group (the instance module's instPick and instMove): each instance's flag, nonzero
// while it is carried with the dragged one. Here for bank 7's room; the instance module reaches
// it through its 16-bit address.
gMem,
    table MAXINST, 0

constants

// The rest of bank 11, after the manager. First the tape module's root and its overlay tape. It
// moves a picture to or from the Microtape, with the display on WAIT (waitList) and the break
// system off, and keeps the tape's directory and its screen, which penISR starts by full
// address. The main bank enters it through tapeCall, with an entry number (TESAVE to TEDIR),
// and at tpPickName for Save's name; it runs with the extend window open, reaching the
// picture's words in banks 0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 9 and 10 through 16-bit addresses, and calls
// nothing outside W and bank 11 but the view module's vwInit. Then the library of masters
// (splib.ac), its root and its overlay library, a master saved as an entry on the tape and an
// entry loaded into a master, whose entries (TELSAVE, TELLOAD) tapeCall runs through the tape's
// stub, tapeEntry. Then Plot (spplot.ac), its root and its overlay plot, the page drawn on the
// plotter, whose entry (TEPLOT) tapeCall runs the same way. Then start-up's gates (spinit.ac's
// initGates), run once between bank 12's initVars and the main bank's init, which start the
// manager, with the hook a failed load goes to (drumFail). Then the menu's census
// (spcensus.ac), which the main bank's actOpen takes as a list opens.
// Then the truss's analysis, the members' forces, a slice a pass, and the readouts, whose list
// is in bank 13: its root stubs, then the overlay truss, with its floating point (spfloat.ac,
// which sptruss.ac includes).
// The main bank enters it at taInit and taTick, the view module at taRedo; it runs with the
// extend window open, reaching the constraint table, the point table, the main bank's words,
// bank 0's and banks 14 and 15's through 16-bit addresses, and calls nothing outside itself.
// Each module here is placed after the banks it reaches but 12 to 15, so that nearly every
// reference it makes to them is a backward one. Then the display of what a lift will take
// (splock.ac); the main bank enters it through showDot and the entries its header names, and
// it calls nothing outside banks 11 and 12. Then a line slot's plan and vectors (spslot.ac), which
// the main bank's writeSlot enters at lnEmit. Last, the overlay table, which the manager reads,
// after the last overlay (truss), as am1 requires.
bank 0d11

#include "sptape.ac"

#include "splib.ac"

#include "spplot.ac"

#include "spinit.ac"

#include "spcensus.ac"

#include "sptruss.ac"

// The marks' ranks, counted again after the constraint table changes: the overlay ranks in W,
// no root words, called by bank 13's mkMarks.
#include "spranks.ac"

// The constraints on size's root words, the runner and the rename.
#include "spsize.ac"

#include "splock.ac"

#include "spslot.ac"

// The masters' texts, for the text module (sptext.ac), which reaches them through their 16-bit
// addresses: mtN of them, mtM naming the master and mtDX, mtDY the offset from its origin; their
// runs packed in mtRun, MTPOOLW words, run t from the word mtRS's entry t names up to the one
// its entry t + 1 names (the text module's txFit). mtM to mtRun is one run, which a picture's
// save writes and its load reads whole after the canvas's (sptape.ac, TPTEXTS).
mtM,
    table NMTEXT, 0
mtDX,
    table NMTEXT, 0
mtDY,
    table NMTEXT, 0
mtSc,
    table NMTEXT, 0
mtCh,
    table NMTEXT, 0
mtW,
    table NMTEXT, 0
mtRS,
    table NMTEXT + 1, 0
mtRun,
    table MTPOOLW, 0

// The masters' digits, a separate run that a save writes in the digits' block (sptape.ac,
// TPDIGITS). First each master's text's anchor, the master index of the point at its center,
// NOPOINT for a plain text; then a set of digits' value and fix, its scalar's at Define. Three
// tables NMTEXT apart, in this order (mtMove, TPDIGITS).
mtAn,
    table NMTEXT, NOPOINT
mtVal,
    table NMTEXT, 0
mtFix,
    table NMTEXT, 0

%%ovtable

constants

// Bank 12 holds the copy of penISR's mailboxes for the main loop (snapshot), the writes made
// between frames (commitFlip and tgtFlip) and the lock mark's arms (clipLock). None is reached
// by the display, but the texts' list after them. Each runs with the extend window open,
// reaching bank 0's and the main bank's words through 16-bit addresses, and calls nothing
// outside bank 12. Placed last, so that every reference it makes to the other banks is a
// backward one. Then the view module (spview.ac), and what a dismember's or a copy's
// sub-instances will call brought into the store (spsub.ac), entered the same way.
bank 0d12
0/

#include "spaux.ac"
#include "spview.ac"
#include "spsub.ac"

constants

// The texts' list, two buffers, each holding per text shown its parameter, y and x words and
// its run, then the halt. The text module (sptext.ac) writes them through their 16-bit
// addresses, and penISR starts the one shown (txGo) after the frame's closing halt; no other
// list is in this bank, so penISR knows the texts' halt by its bank. After the bank's
// literals, last, so that only the bank's free words lie past txBufB.
txBufA,
    table TXLISTW, 0
txBufB,
    table TXLISTW, 0

// Bank 13's data. The truss's incidences, whose words hold the map until the analysis's
// directions pass writes them (taInc, taMap), which the truss module (sptruss.ac) reaches through
// 16-bit addresses; the members' taMI and taMK and their coefficients tdC are in bank 3, the
// rollers' axes, taAX, and the snapshot, taSnap, in bank 14. Then the readouts' list (roList),
// which penISR starts by full address, per readout a parameter, a y and an x word and at most
// three of characters, one for each entry at most, then UNSTABLE's six words and the halt.
bank 0d13
0/

taInc,
taMap,
    table MAXPTS, 0
roList,
    table NCON * 6 + 7, 0

// The lines on the solver's points (cBuild), which the main bank's conRedraw reads too, through
// their 16-bit address. In bank 13 for bank 9's room.
cLines,
    table MAXLINES, 0

// After the data, the constraints' marks (spmarks.ac). The constraint module enters them at
// mkMarks and mkNear by their 16-bit addresses; they run with the extend window open, reaching
// bank 8's words, the constraint table and bank 0's fixList through 16-bit addresses, and call
// nothing outside bank 13.

// A mark on one line stands beside it (cMkPos). Per type, indexed like cNPts, where the entry
// names its line, 1 when in words 1 and 2 (H, L, a Beam's B, a Load's W), 2 when in words 2 and
// 3 after its point (X, N), 0 for a mark not on one line.
cLnTab,
    0
    1                   // CTHL
    1                   // CTHP
    0                   // CTF
    0                   // CTEQ
    1                   // CTLEN
    0                   // CTPAR
    0                   // CTPERP
    2                   // CTMID
    2                   // CTON
    0                   // CTONC
    0                   // CTATT
    1                   // CTBEAM
    1                   // CTLOAD
    0                   // CTROLL
    0                   // CTDES
    0                   // CTDIST
    0                   // CTCHG
    0                   // CTGAP
    0                   // CTSAME
    0                   // CTFULL
    0                   // CTINCH
    0                   // CTSZNUM

#include "spmarks.ac"

// Per direction k, the x of a one-line mark's offset from its place on the line, in thousandths
// of the distance (cMkPos); its y, and what the directions are, is bank 9's cOfY.
cOfX,
    0
    -0d383
    -0d707
    0d924
    0d1000
    0d924
    0d707
    0d383

// Then the line search, which finds the nearest line to the target's center, and in Line,
// Circle and Move the second nearest and the two lines' crossing, swept a slice a pass. The
// main bank's placeLock
// enters it at lineSearch; it runs with the extend window open, reaching the point and line
// tables and the main bank's variables through 16-bit addresses, and calls nothing outside bank
// 13. Placed after the banks it reaches, so that every reference it makes to them is a backward
// one.
#include "spsearch.ac"

// Then the arcs through the magnifier's view (spvarc.ac). The arc module enters it at vaSlot
// and vaBand by their 16-bit addresses; it runs with the extend window
// open, reaching the arc module's words, the slots and bank 12's view module through 16-bit
// addresses, and calls nothing outside banks 12 and 13 (the clipper, through vwClipX).
#include "spvarc.ac"

constants

// The truss's direct solve, banks 14 and 15, data only, reached by sptruss.ac through 16-bit
// addresses and written before each is read, so not on the tape. Per unknown its
// row's base address and first coupled unknown (tdU), 1/D (tdRD) and the right side, then the
// displacements (tdY); per member e_x and e_y (tdE); each roller joint's unit axis, a_x then
// a_y (taAX), and the snapshot taCheck compares (taSnap), TATABW words the two; then the
// matrix's profile, run on through bank 15 (tdK, tdK2). Numbers are three words (spfloat.ac).
// The snapshot is the one table read before it is written: a check after taInitOv, which
// zeroes its end (taSnapE), finds the length changed whatever its words hold.
// The library's entry buffer, lbEBuf, LBBUFW words from the bank's start, shares them: a save
// or a load writes it within one call of the overlay library (splib.ac), first setting
// taReset, so that the truss starts again from its map rather than resume on a spoiled profile.
bank 0d14
0/

lbEBuf,
tdU,
    table TANU * 2
tdRD,
    table TANU * 3
tdY,
    table TANU * 3
tdE,
    table NCON * 6
taAX,
    table TANJ * 6
taSnap,
    table NCON * 0d8
tdK,
    table 0d4096 - TANU * 0d8 - NCON * 6 - TATABW

bank 0d15
0/

tdK2,
    table 0d4096

bank 0
start boot
